{"type":"text","timestamp":1794379907400,"sessionID":"ses_e36a1605fffeQa463ZF52q8gD3","part":{"id":"prt_1c960812d001L5mSuJI6dpvp27","messageID":"msg_1c9606d16001JWd3eWLFsys1nP","sessionID":"ses_e36a1605fffeQa463ZF52q8gD3","type":"text","text":"<think>Only /tmp/opencode is allowed as external dir, but it's root-owned and not writable. Let me check if I can write there... \"Permission denied\" when creating venv. Maybe I can chmod? Not owner (root). Hmm.\n\nAlternative: work within /workspace (create a venv there, gitignored). That's allowed since it's the workspace. But I should avoid polluting the repo. I could create the venv in /workspace/.venv and add to .gitignore, then delete it at the end. Or use pip install --user into home dir (~/.local). Home is /run/home which is writable by node.\n\nLet me try pip install --user flask.\n\nAlso, the npm cache is at /tmp/llmlab-deps/npm (per npm error log path) — a read-only cache. npm ci will use it.\n\nLet me try installing python packages to user site.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794379907373,"end":1794379907395}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794379909628,"sessionID":"ses_e36a1605fffeQa463ZF52q8gD3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c96079f77454b9791f1a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && pip install --user -q flask==3.1.3 gunicorn==26.2.0 2>&1 | tail -3; python3 -c \"import flask, itsdangerous, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\""},"output":"<string>:1: DeprecationWarning: The '__version__' attribute is deprecated and will be removed in Flask 3.2. Use feature detection or 'importlib.metadata.version(\"flask\")' instead.\n<string>:1: DeprecationWarning: The '__version__' attribute is deprecated and will be removed in ItsDangerous 2.3. Use feature detection or 'importlib.metadata.version(\"itsdangerous\")' instead.\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, itsdangerous, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\n                                                                                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAttributeError: module 'werkzeug' has no attribute '__version__'\n","metadata":{"output":"<string>:1: DeprecationWarning: The '__version__' attribute is deprecated and will be removed in Flask 3.2. Use feature detection or 'importlib.metadata.version(\"flask\")' instead.\n<string>:1: DeprecationWarning: The '__version__' attribute is deprecated and will be removed in ItsDangerous 2.3. Use feature detection or 'importlib.metadata.version(\"itsdangerous\")' instead.\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, itsdangerous, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\n                                                                                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAttributeError: module 'werkzeug' has no attribute '__version__'\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && pip install --user -q flask==3.1.3 gunicorn==26.2.0 2>&1 | tail -3; python3 -c \"import flask, itsdangerous, werkzeug; print(flask.__version__, itsdangerous.__version__, werkzeug.__version__)\"","time":{"start":1794379907384,"end":1794379909530}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c96081310014WXR84XPLwEeOC","sessionID":"ses_e36a1605fffeQa463ZF52q8gD3","messageID":"msg_1c9606d16001JWd3eWLFsys1nP"}}
