{"type":"text","timestamp":1794380719344,"sessionID":"ses_e36a1605fffeQa463ZF52q8gD3","part":{"id":"prt_1c96ce4da001hD1dGXdwF64ziP","messageID":"msg_1c96cd7cb001a8eYFY7jg8OGJu","sessionID":"ses_e36a1605fffeQa463ZF52q8gD3","type":"text","text":"<think>Wait — send_from_directory is safe against path traversal (werkzeug's safe_join). So dropping the manual resolve check is fine.\n\nNow let me quickly smoke-test the backend. First run it and curl endpoints.\n\nLet me start the server in the background with a temp data dir under /workspace/data (or a test data dir). Since /tmp isn't writable, use /workspace/.testdata? Hmm, the app's default DATA_DIR is /workspace/data which is what Docker would use. For testing, I can use DATA_DIR=/workspace/data (fine, it's the real runtime dir; the DB will be created). Let me just use the default so I also verify the default path works.\n\nLet me run the server.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794380719322,"end":1794380719340}}}
